  "source": "GE Vernova Multilin, \"EPM 6000/6000T Power Meter Instruction Manual\", software revision 1.17, GEK-106558G (1601-0215-A8)",
  "sources": [{"title": "EPM 6000/6000T Power Meter Instruction Manual", "version": "GEK-106558G", "url": "https://www.gevernova.com/grid-solutions/sites/default/files/resources/products/manuals/epm/epm6000-a8-GEV.pdf", "note": "Appendix B, Modbus register map"}],
  "notes": [
    "All registers are holding registers (FC03 read, FC06/FC10 write). Addresses here are the zero-based hex addresses of the manual; the manual's decimal register numbers are one higher (e.g. 0x03E7 = register 1000).",
    "32-bit values and floats span two registers with the high-order half first.",
    "Factory settings in normal mode are 57600 baud, address 1, Modbus RTU, 8 bits, no parity. For 5 seconds after power-up the RS-485 port also answers at 9600 baud, address 1, and keeps those settings for 5 minutes once used.",
    "Energy registers are integers whose scale, digit count and decimal places follow the power and energy format setting (0x7535). Reset the energy after changing that format.",
    "The 3-phase power readings at 0x0383-0x0388 are updated every 6 cycles; the other readings every 60 cycles. THD reads 65535 when it is not available (needs the THD option).",
    "Not in this map: the individual harmonic magnitudes, the meter programming and encryption blocks, programmable settings and the 12-bit readings block (0x9C40-0x9CA3)."
  ],
